  "omitted": [
    {
      "name": "snap counts",
      "reason": "The snap file is a postgame count. Last week's snaps are already inside the next week's EPA, so they are not a separate pregame input."
    },
    {
      "name": "closing spread, moneyline, and total",
      "reason": "Market numbers. The closing spread is scored as a comparison and is not a feature."
    },
    {
      "name": "current-game participation",
      "reason": "Who played the snaps is known after the game. The screen uses the depth chart and the injury report instead."
    },
    {
      "name": "coaches, referees, and division flags",
      "reason": "They are on the schedule. A separate flag per coach would memorize clubs. They are not aspect weights."
    },
    {
      "name": "relocation priors",
      "reason": "Oakland's 2019 rating is not copied onto Las Vegas in 2020, and San Diego is not copied onto the Chargers. Those week-1 handoffs stay at the league rate. The published EPA blend does the same."
    }
  ],
  "personnel_rule": "Expected starter is the first offense-chart quarterback who is not Out or Doubtful. Weekly charts are the chart for that week. Daily charts, from 2025 on, use the last snapshot dated before gameday. Injury rows with a timestamp after gameday are dropped. Seasons whose injury file has no timestamp keep the week's report. out_diff counts players ruled Out, except kickers, punters, and long snappers. qb_edge is that starter's career pass EPA from 1999 on, shrunk with 300 prior plays toward zero, home minus away. Same-week games do not use each other's plays, matching the published EPA week cut.",
  "static_frozen_note": "Equal-weight ridge fit on 2018-2023 only, then frozen. Those six seasons are in-sample for the static row. 2024-2026 are a comparison. The static row cannot replace the dynamic model after the check is known."
}
